# Block package lifecycle scripts (preinstall/install/postinstall) during
# `yarn install`.
#
# Lifecycle scripts are the execution vector for npm supply-chain attacks: a
# compromised package runs arbitrary code on the machine that installs it,
# before any of its code is ever imported. The August 2026 Shai-Hulud worm
# (keyv, cacheable-request and ~434 packages via propagation) shipped its
# credential stealer exactly this way, through an injected `preinstall`.
#
# .devcontainer/devcontainer.json sets NPM_CONFIG_IGNORE_SCRIPTS, but yarn 1
# does not read NPM_CONFIG_* variables, so that only ever covered `npm`. This
# file is what covers `yarn`, which is the package manager this project builds
# with. Verified: `yarn config get ignore-scripts` reports true, and install
# reports "Ignored scripts due to flag".
#
# Note the bare `ignore-scripts true` form is required — the per-command
# `--install.ignore-scripts true` form does not register as this config key.
#
# Two dependencies declare postinstall scripts, and both are safe to skip:
#   esbuild@0.21.5   install.js only validates the platform binary, which is
#                    shipped inside the @esbuild/linux-x64 package itself.
#                    Verified working at 0.21.5 with scripts blocked.
#   core-js-pure     prints a donation notice.
# A clean `yarn install --frozen-lockfile && yarn build && yarn test` passes
# with this enabled (234 tests, 19 suites).
#
# If a future dependency genuinely needs its install script, run that one
# install with `yarn install --ignore-scripts false` rather than deleting this
# file — and read the script first.
ignore-scripts true
